  "worked_solution": "Isolating the eighth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(2-5x)^{8}+7 & <3 \\\\ 2(2-5x)^{8} & <-4 \\\\ (2-5x)^{8} & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(2-5x)^{8}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(8)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality.",
